{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)"],"title":"Type Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Methods"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"enum","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"role":"symbol","title":"EntityCollapse","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence14EntityCollapseO","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Why the hook takes the whole collection","anchor":"Why-the-hook-takes-the-whole-collection","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A per-ID resolver would only handle half the problem. Rows sharing an "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are one failure mode; the other is a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"singleton"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — an entity an app holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly one of, such as a settings record. Created independently on two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fresh installs, two singletons have "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"different"}]},{"type":"text","text":" UUIDs, so nothing groups"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them and no ID-keyed resolver can ever see the conflict. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"([E]) -> [E]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" hook covers both, plus general garbage collection, with one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The determinism requirement","anchor":"The-determinism-requirement","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A resolver must be a pure function of "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"replicated content"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"persistentModelID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", never a local timestamp, never array position. Every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"device must compute the same survivor set from the same rows. A resolver"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that doesn’t reintroduces the mutual-tombstone loss the write path is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"designed to avoid: two devices pick different survivors, each tombstones the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other’s, and after sync "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"both"}]},{"type":"text","text":" rows are gone."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It must also be idempotent — "},{"code":"collapse(collapse(rows))","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" must keep the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"IDs as "},{"code":"collapse(rows)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". This is checked with an "},{"code":"assert","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in debug builds."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Collapse removes IDs, not rows","anchor":"Collapse-removes-IDs-not-rows","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A resolver’s output is read as ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the set of IDs that should exist and what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each should contain","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":". An ID the resolver drops is deleted, including every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row carrying it. Several rows that share a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"surviving","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ID are all updated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the survivor’s value, and none of them is deleted.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"That asymmetry is deliberate, and it is the whole reason the singleton case","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is the one this hook really solves. Deleting an ID is safe because ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"replicated: every device independently computes the same set of doomed IDs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and issues the same deletions. Deleting one of several rows that share an ID","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" safe — nothing replicated distinguishes them, so two devices can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pick different physical rows to keep, each tombstones the other’s, and both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are lost.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Rows sharing an ID need no deletion anyway: writes already converge across","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"every matching row and reads already collapse to one value per ID (see","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","isActive":true},{"text":"), so duplicates cost storage and nothing else.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse"},"references":{"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityDB":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitydb","role":"symbol","title":"EntityDB","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityDB"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A generic ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@ModelActor"},{"text":" that reads and writes any ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityDB"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityCollapse/byID(preferring:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse\/byid(preferring:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)","role":"symbol","title":"byID(preferring:)","abstract":[{"text":"Collapses rows sharing an ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" down to one, keeping the winner of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"choose","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Rows with unique IDs pass through untouched.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"byID"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"E"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"preferring"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"E"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kin